cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its analysis pipeline, please cite it as below."
title: "materials-mlip-research: chemistry-stratified value of selective abstention for ML interatomic-potential crystal-stability screening (MT29)"
abstract: >-
  CPU-only, real-data audit of frozen Matbench Discovery predictions (four ML
  interatomic potentials on 256,963 WBM structures) testing whether the benefit of
  confidence-based selective abstention for the binary crystal-stability decision is
  chemistry-dependent, with matched-yield, leave-one-element-out, acquisition-round,
  committee-variance, shuffle-null, and BH-FDR/Holm multiplicity controls.
type: software
